examples.question_text:
Which graph, A or B, could represent $y=4^{-x}$? Explain your choice.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{scope}
\draw[black,->] (-1.5,0)--(1.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.3)--(0,3.1) node[above] {$y$};
\node[anchor=east] at (-1.5,2.7) {A};
\draw[graphBlue,thick,<->,smooth,samples=70,domain=-1.4:0.72,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(\x*ln(4))});
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(5,0)}]
\draw[black,->] (-1.5,0)--(1.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.3)--(0,3.1) node[above] {$y$};
\node[anchor=east] at (-1.5,2.7) {B};
\draw[graphBlue,thick,<->,smooth,samples=70,domain=-0.72:1.4,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(-\x*ln(4))});
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which equation, A–C, could represent the graph shown?

A. $y=3x^{2}+4$
B. $y=-3x^{2}+4$
C. $y=3x^{2}-4$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-2,0)--(2.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,9.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black] (-0.08,4)--(0.08,4);
\node[anchor=east,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.12,4) {$4$};
\draw[graphBlue,thick,<->,smooth,samples=70,domain=-1.25:1.25,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*(\x)*(\x)+4});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
